title: 'Coprime paths: the nine-edge threshold, linear bounds, and reproducible evidence'
version: 2026.10.20
authors:
- given-names: Alexander Richard
  family-names: Towell
  orcid: https://orcid.org/0000-0001-6443-9897
  affiliation: Southern Illinois University Edwardsville
abstract: The coprime graph on 1,...,17 forces a monochromatic simple nine-edge path
  in every two-edge-coloring, while a complete coloring at 16 avoids one. The upper
  bound combines a written extremal classification with independently checked finite
  host lemmas. The record also preserves earlier independently recertified seven-
  and eight-edge thresholds, linear bounds, an author-revised manuscript, and clearly
  separated exploratory findings. Human mathematical review and novelty assessment
  remain incomplete.
